user-command-missing-start = The start folder is missing. Set start-in to a folder that exists in user-commands.toml.
user-command-program-missing = The program was not found. Fix the program path in user-commands.toml.
user-command-too-long = The command line is over 32,000 UTF-16 units. Use the marked-list placeholder in user-commands.toml for many files.
user-command-shell-placeholder = A command that starts a shell cannot use placeholders. Remove them from the command in user-commands.toml.
user-command-marked-not-whole = The marked placeholder must be a whole argument. Give it its own argument in user-commands.toml.
user-command-bad-start-in = The start folder must be one value. Fix start-in in user-commands.toml.
user-command-unknown-program = The program name cannot be verified, so placeholders are not allowed. Write the full program path in user-commands.toml.
user-command-terminal-placeholder = A Windows Terminal command cannot use placeholders. Put the folder in start-in and write wt -d . in user-commands.toml.
user-command-spawn-error = Could not start the command ({ $error }). Close some programs and run the command again.
user-command-start-error = The command did not start ({ $error }). Check the command in user-commands.toml and run it again.
user-command-list-root = Could not find your local app data or home folder for the list file. Check that your user profile is complete and run the command again.
user-command-list-folder-error = Could not prepare the folder for list files ({ $error }). Check that your profile folder is writable and run the command again.
user-command-list-folder-unsafe = The folder for list files is not a private, real folder. Remove any link there or make it private to you, then run the command again.
user-command-list-line-break = A marked file name contains a line break, so it cannot go in a list file. Rename the file and run the command again.
user-command-list-file-error = Could not write the list file ({ $error }). Free some disk space and run the command again.
user-command-pid-file-error = Could not write the process file next to the list file ({ $error }). Free some disk space and run the command again.
user-command-list-marker = The marked-list placeholder could not be filled in. Give it its own argument in user-commands.toml and run the command again.
user-command-file-syntax = user-commands.toml cannot be read ({ $detail }). Fix line { $line } of user-commands.toml.
user-command-file-empty = The { $field } value is empty. Fill it in on line { $line } of user-commands.toml.
user-command-file-duplicate-name = The name { $name } is already used on line { $first }. Rename the command on line { $line } of user-commands.toml.
user-command-file-program-placeholder = The program cannot contain the { $placeholder } placeholder. Write the program without placeholders on line { $line } of user-commands.toml.
user-command-file-unclosed-quote = The args value leaves a quotation mark open. Close it on line { $line } of user-commands.toml.
user-command-file-lone-brace = A closing brace has no opening brace. Write two closing braces for a literal brace on line { $line } of user-commands.toml.
user-command-file-unclosed-brace = An opening brace is not closed. Close the placeholder or write two opening braces on line { $line } of user-commands.toml.
user-command-file-unknown-placeholder = { $name } is not a placeholder. Use a known placeholder on line { $line } of user-commands.toml.
user-command-file-marked-not-whole = The marked placeholder must be a whole argument. Give it its own argument on line { $line } of user-commands.toml.
user-command-file-start-in-placeholder = The start-in value cannot use the { $placeholder } placeholder. Use only folder or other-folder on line { $line } of user-commands.toml.
user-command-file-key-not-one = A shortcut must be one key. Fix the key on line { $line } of user-commands.toml.
user-command-file-not-a-key = { $key } is not a key. Fix the key on line { $line } of user-commands.toml.
user-command-file-key-modifier = { $key } is a modifier alone. Add another key on line { $line } of user-commands.toml.
user-command-file-key-bare = { $key } is a bare letter or digit. Add Ctrl or Alt on line { $line } of user-commands.toml.
user-command-file-key-reserved = { $key } is reserved by the operating system. Choose another key on line { $line } of user-commands.toml.
user-command-file-shell-placeholder = A command that starts a shell cannot use the { $placeholder } placeholder. Remove it from line { $line } of user-commands.toml.
user-command-file-shell-default-start = A command that starts a shell needs a literal start-in, because the default start folder counts as a placeholder. Add start-in to the command on line { $line } of user-commands.toml.
user-command-file-terminal-placeholder = A Windows Terminal command cannot use placeholders. Put the folder in start-in and write wt -d . on line { $line } of user-commands.toml.
user-command-file-unknown-program = The program name cannot be verified, so placeholders are not allowed. Write the full program path on line { $line } of user-commands.toml.

